WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.830
Jack: To improve skills and grow
professionally it is important

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.830
to get feedback especially on
how we communicate to others.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.770
As we have already said, it helps us to
know that others understand what we are

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:13.990
communicating, enabling them to respond.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.190
Leah: Feedback is a vital part of
any communication process and project

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.750
managers, team leaders, instructors
and coaches develop the skill of giving

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.220
feedback throughout their career.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.690
They are also involved in receiving
feedback as well as this is an

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:34.080
important way of sharing information and
communicating within a work environment.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.110
Jack: Feedback should be seen as
a positive thing as it can be used

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.800
to develop communication skills.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.440
Feedback should be listened to
actively and analysed to help

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.169
improve future communications.

00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:50.050
It can provide positive criticism and
allows everyone to improve their focus.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.749
It can also create a healthy
communication flow up and down

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.270
the levels of an organisation.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.250
Leah: Constructive feedback is
an excellent tool which can help

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.519
optimise the communication process
and increase transparency and trust.

00:01:05.039 --> 00:01:09.789
Clear and honest communication flow
within a team, saves time and subsequently

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:13.740
money and can reduce errors caused
by miscommunication to a minimum.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.200
Jack: By seeing that the feedback is
there to help projects succeed, it

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.950
can also motivate the team members.

00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:24.480
Readily seeking feedback and ways to
improve, can help show the openness

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:26.690
to other ideas that may be beneficial.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.559
It can also showcase unforeseen problems
and suggest alternative solutions.

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:36.140
Leah: But saying that feedback that is
negative or feedback that is not specific

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.740
can be unhelpful as it can demotivate.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.800
The feedback should not just dismiss
the communication but should start

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.990
the process of engagement and debate.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:50.050
Those giving feedback especially in a
work-based situation should themselves

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.850
become part of the problem-solving
process if the opportunity arises.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.770
Jack: As we have previously discussed
listening is an important part of the

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:02.289
communication process and listening and
acting on feedback gives opportunities

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:03.870
for everyone to grow their skills.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.740
Feedback is essential in communication
to know whether the recipient has

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.180
understood the message in the same terms
as intended by the sender and whether

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.720
he agrees to that message or not.

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:20.090
Leah: Feedback also enables us to evaluate
the effectiveness of our message and

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:24.600
if that feedback is timely then further
communications can be made to help

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.480
clarify any miscommunication or emissions.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.510
Therefore, providing immediate
feedback enables people to better

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.190
learn from any mistakes they make.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:38.400
However, if they communicate effectively
to begin with, it's still valuable

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.750
to provide feedback instantly, as
it reinforces that effectiveness and

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.959
motivates by affirming competence.

